SDE: de-duplicate the plane format list, which crashes every Wayland compositor.

Weston 14 aborts on this device the instant it reads a plane's formats:

    GL renderer: zink Vulkan 1.3(Adreno 7c+ Gen 3 (MESA_TURNIP))
    Using GL renderer
    Assertion failed: !weston_drm_format_array_find_format(formats, format)
        (../libweston/drm-formats.c: weston_drm_format_array_add_format: 131)

Note where it dies. This is AFTER the DRM backend came up, after gl-renderer
loaded, after EGL reported dmabuf modifier support, and after the GPU was
selected and announced. Weston had the Adreno running through zink/Turnip and
threw the whole thing away over a duplicate entry in a list.

THE DUPLICATE IS REAL, measured on the running device:

    drm_info /dev/dri/card0   ->  40 format entries, 39 unique
                                  ABGR8888 (0x34324241) appears TWICE

WHY

sde_populate_formats() de-duplicates against only the PREVIOUS entry:

    /* assume base formats grouped together */
    if (fourcc_format != format_list->fourcc_format) {

That assumption does not hold for this panel. Its list is

    ARGB8888, ABGR8888, RGBA8888, ABGR8888, BGRA8888, ...

so ABGR8888 at index 1 and index 3 are not adjacent, the comparison against the
previous entry passes, and it is emitted a second time. That duplicate then
goes straight into the plane's format array and therefore into the IN_FORMATS
blob that sde-advertise-in-formats.patch publishes.

Nothing in the kernel cares. Every Wayland compositor does, because
drm_format_array is a set and Weston asserts that property.

THE FIX

Scan the whole array already built rather than just the last entry. O(n^2) on
a list of 40, run once per plane at probe, so the cost is irrelevant.

Deliberately NOT touched: the `if (pixel_modifiers)` branch above. There the
same fourcc legitimately repeats once per modifier, and de-duplicating it would
be wrong.

VERIFY AFTER FLASHING

    drm_info /dev/dri/card0 | grep -A40 IN_FORMATS | grep -c ABGR8888   # 1, not 2
    weston --backend=drm-backend.so --tty=1                             # must not abort

--- a/techpack/display/msm/sde/sde_formats.c
+++ b/techpack/display/msm/sde/sde_formats.c
@@ -1285,7 +1285,8 @@
 		uint64_t *pixel_modifiers,
 		uint32_t pixel_formats_max)
 {
-	uint32_t i, fourcc_format;
+	uint32_t i, j, fourcc_format;
+	bool duplicate;
 
 	if (!format_list || !pixel_formats)
 		return 0;
@@ -1301,8 +1302,23 @@
 			pixel_formats[i] = format_list->fourcc_format;
 			pixel_modifiers[i++] = format_list->modifier;
 		} else {
-			/* assume base formats grouped together */
-			if (fourcc_format != format_list->fourcc_format) {
+			/*
+			 * Do NOT assume identical fourccs are adjacent. This
+			 * panel lists ABGR8888 at both index 1 and index 3, so
+			 * comparing against only the previous entry emitted it
+			 * twice, the duplicate reached the IN_FORMATS blob, and
+			 * Weston aborted on it. Scan what was built so far.
+			 */
+			duplicate = false;
+			for (j = 0; j < i; ++j) {
+				if (pixel_formats[j] ==
+						format_list->fourcc_format) {
+					duplicate = true;
+					break;
+				}
+			}
+
+			if (!duplicate) {
 				fourcc_format = format_list->fourcc_format;
 				pixel_formats[i++] = fourcc_format;
 			}
